# Performance Analysis Report

## Executive Summary

**Total Issues Found**: 86 performance issues across 12 source files
- 🔴 **Critical**: 8 issues (socket exhaustion, O(n²) algorithms, regex compilation abuse)
- 🟡 **Moderate**: 31 issues (boxing, unnecessary allocations, reflection in hot paths)
- ℹ️ **Info**: 47 issues (best practices, minor optimizations)

**Top Priorities**: Fix regex abuse in MarkdownStripper, HttpClient instantiation patterns, and string concatenation in hot paths.

## Findings by File

### TextProcessing/UnitFormatter.cs
**🟡 Moderate Issues:**
- Line 15: `struct UnitPrefix` lacks `IEquatable<T>` — boxing on equality checks
- Line 60-66: `.Aggregate()` with `.Replace()` creates 16 intermediate string allocations
- Line 64: `char.ToString()` allocation per iteration
- Line 224-230: `ContainsKey` + indexer instead of `TryGetValue`

**ℹ️ Info Issues:**
- Line 75, 102, 159, 172, 185: Lists without capacity hints
- Line 101-106: String concatenation in loop (ConvertBatch method)
- Line 158, 172, 185: Unsealed leaf classes (should be `sealed`)

**Fix Recommendations:**
```csharp
// Add IEquatable<T> to UnitPrefix
public struct UnitPrefix : IEquatable<UnitPrefix>
{
    public bool Equals(UnitPrefix other) => 
        Symbol == other.Symbol && Name == other.Name && Factor == other.Factor;

    public override bool Equals(object? obj) => 
        obj is UnitPrefix other && Equals(other);

    public override int GetHashCode() => 
        HashCode.Combine(Symbol, Name, Factor);
}

// Replace .Aggregate() with single-pass StringBuilder
public string ExpandPrefixSymbols(string displayValue)
{
    var sb = new StringBuilder(displayValue);
    foreach (var prefix in Prefixes)
    {
        sb.Replace(prefix.Symbol, prefix.Name);
    }
    return sb.ToString();
}

// Use TryGetValue
if (Registry.TryGetValue(locale, out var ordinalizer))
    return ordinalizer;
```

### TextProcessing/TextTruncation.cs
**🟡 Moderate Issues:**
- Lines 15-18: `List<char>[]` instead of `ReadOnlySpan<char>` or string constants
- Line 32: Double allocation — `value[..n].TrimEnd()` creates two strings
- Line 35: `.Contains` on `List<char>` (O(n)) instead of HashSet
- Line 84, 90: `Substring` instead of `AsSpan` (inconsistent with other truncators)

**ℹ️ Info Issues:**
- Line 107: `params` array without single-argument overload
- Line 120: List without capacity hint

**Fix Recommendations:**
```csharp
// Replace List<char> with ReadOnlySpan<char>
public static class TruncationSymbols
{
    public static ReadOnlySpan<char> PunctuationChars => new[] { '.', ',', ';', ':', '!', '?' };
    // or use string constants: ".,;:!?"
}

// Fix double allocation
var span = value.AsSpan(0, Math.Min(maxLength, value.Length));
var trimmed = span.TrimEnd();
// Remove punctuation from the end
while (!trimmed.IsEmpty && PunctuationChars.Contains(trimmed[^1]))
    trimmed = trimmed[..^1];
return new string(trimmed) + ellipsis;

// Add single-argument overload for params method
public static string Apply(string value, int maxLength, ITruncator truncator) =>
    truncator.Truncate(value, maxLength);
```

### TextProcessing/TemplateEngine.cs
**🔴 Critical Issues:**
- Lines 22, 30, 43, 73: Per-call `Regex` instantiation — should use `[GeneratedRegex]` or static compiled
- Line 53: String concatenation in loop (O(n²))
- Line 58: New `Dictionary` per iteration + copying entire context

**🟡 Moderate Issues:**
- Line 98-100: Reflection `GetProperty()` in hot path without caching
- Line 114: `.Any()` forces enumeration just to check non-empty
- Line 121: String concatenation in loop

**Fix Recommendations:**
```csharp
// Use GeneratedRegex (.NET 7+)
[GeneratedRegex(@"\{\{.+?\}\}")]
private static partial Regex CleanupPattern();

[GeneratedRegex(@"\{\{#if\s+(\w+)\}\}([\s\S]*?)\{\{/if\}\}")]
private static partial Regex ConditionalPattern();

// Or use static compiled regex for older versions
private static readonly Regex ConditionalPattern = 
    new(@"\{\{#if\s+(\w+)\}\}([\s\S]*?)\{\{/if\}\}", RegexOptions.Compiled);

// Replace string concatenation with StringBuilder
var output = new StringBuilder();
foreach (var item in items)
{
    // Clone context more efficiently
    var iterContext = context.ToDictionary(kvp => kvp.Key, kvp => kvp.Value);
    iterContext["item"] = item;
    iterContext["index"] = index;

    output.Append(ReplaceVariables(body, iterContext));
    index++;
}

// Cache reflection info
private static readonly ConcurrentDictionary<Type, PropertyInfo[]> PropertyCache = new();

private object? GetPropertyValue(object obj, string propertyName)
{
    var type = obj.GetType();
    var properties = PropertyCache.GetOrAdd(type, t => t.GetProperties());
    var prop = properties.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == propertyName);
    return prop?.GetValue(obj);
}
```

### TextProcessing/SlugGenerator.cs
**🔴 Critical Issues:**
- Lines 39-52: 13 per-call static `Regex.Replace` calls — should use compiled patterns

**🟡 Moderate Issues:**
- Line 30: `.ToLower()` without culture + allocation
- Lines 33-36: Sequential `.Replace()` calls (8 allocations)
- Line 75: `.ToList()` + `.Contains()` (O(n)) in loop

**Fix Recommendations:**
